-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I33: I32's CONTROL, and the row that keeps a
-- constraint-aware comparison from warning on code that is correct.  The two
-- declarations name the same two constraints in opposite order over
-- alpha-equivalent bodies, so the schemes AGREE and S2-IMPORT-DIFFER's "not
-- alpha-equivalent" antecedent is false: this cell must be silent on all three
-- verbs.
--
-- Without it, a comparison that pairs constraints POSITIONALLY passes I32 and turns
-- every reordered-but-identical declaration in the tree into a warning -- the
-- false-positive direction, which no ACCEPT/REJECT column can see because the
-- program still compiles and still prints the same value.
--
-- The resolution is I32's: the method dispatches at `Box`, printing `iface`.
import ifc.{Taggable, Box(..)}
import prov.{tagOf}

main = println (tagOf (Box 1) 2 3)
